Product Architecture is the scheme by which functional elements of the product are organized in order to implement the interaction of product elements. This strategy is a cirucular when the intent is to make the product technical reusable for multiple loops. Here, the designer should understand the marketplace, customer target, and the product variety of the different loops to meet the needs of companies and users. In particular, by determinating the details of the product functions the designers will defined "which components must be changed to achive a desired change to a functional element of the product" (Ulrich, 1995).